  </section>

  <!-- How it works -->
  <section id="how" class="section bg-paper" aria-labelledby="how-h">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:items-end">
        <h2 id="how-h" class="h2 lg:col-span-7">From one card to a national programme</h2>
        <p class="lead lg:col-span-5">Our tests are simple, affordable and usable outside specialised laboratories, so that molecular diagnosis can reach everyone.</p>
      </div>
      <ol class="steps mt-12">
        <li>
          <img src="/assets/img/site-sample.webp" width="1000" height="1000" alt="The open card seen from above: a dried blood spot inside its dashed collection circle, above a barcode and sample code." loading="lazy" decoding="async">
          <p class="label">One card</p>
          <h3 class="h3">A spot of blood, dried on a card.</h3>
          <p>That is the whole sample: a finger prick and a card. No needle, no tube, no cold chain on the way to the testing centre.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <img src="/assets/img/site-batch.webp" width="1000" height="1000" alt="The same card, now closed, set down in a grid of many others that each carry the Lightening Lives logo and a barcode." loading="lazy" decoding="async">
          <p class="label">One batch</p>
          <h3 class="h3">From card to result without a DNA extraction step.</h3>
          <p>A small punch from the spot goes straight into the reaction. Many cards run at once, on standard PCR equipment.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <img src="/assets/img/site-map.webp" width="1000" height="1000" alt="Thousands of cards laid out in the shape of India, seen from straight above. The states we have worked in are marked in green, and Delhi, Maharashtra, Jharkhand, Telangana and Tamil Nadu are named." loading="lazy" decoding="async">
          <p class="label">One programme</p>
          <h3 class="h3">Built for screening at the scale of a nation.</h3>
          <p>Population and newborn screening at 15 sites in nine states and Delhi, with test details captured on a mobile app as it happens.</p>
        </li>
      </ol>
      <a class="link mt-10" href="/technology/">How the technology works
        {{ arrow | safe }}
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Why -->
  <section id="why" class="section" aria-labelledby="why-h">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:items-end">
        <h2 id="why-h" class="h2 lg:col-span-7">Molecular diagnostics without the limits of conventional testing</h2>
        <p class="lead lg:col-span-5">Conventional genetic tests need venous blood, a cold chain, a specialist laboratory and a second test to confirm. So they rarely reach the people who need them most.</p>
      </div>
      <ul class="why mt-12">
        <li><h3>A spot of blood, not a tube</h3><p>A finger prick onto a card. No venepuncture, no EDTA tube, no pre-processing.</p></li>
        <li><h3>Room temperature, not a cold chain</h3><p>Cards keep and travel at room temperature, so samples can come from anywhere a health worker can reach.</p></li>
        <li><h3>Screening and confirmation in one</h3><p>One test does both, so a positive result needs no second test and no second visit.*</p></li>
        <li><h3>Extraction-free molecular diagnostics</h3><p>No separate DNA extraction step, which saves a laboratory time and reagents.*</p></li>
        <li><h3>From birth</h3><p>Newborns can be tested at birth. Conventional confirmatory tests wait 72 hours.*</p></li>
        <li><h3>Minimal laboratory infrastructure</h3><p>Standard PCR equipment and a gel tank. No specialised laboratory.</p></li>
        <li><h3>High-throughput, automation-friendly</h3><p>Many cards in one run, on a workflow that can be automated.</p></li>
        <li><h3>For one patient or a whole district</h3><p>Designed for a diagnosis in a clinic and for large-scale public health programmes.</p></li>
      </ul>
      <p class="footnote">* Where applicable for developed assays.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Portfolio -->
  <section id="tests" class="section bg-paper" aria-labelledby="tests-h">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:items-end">
        <h2 id="tests-h" class="h2 lg:col-span-7">Our diagnostic portfolio</h2>
        <p class="lead lg:col-span-5">Four kinds of genetic test, in two families so far, with more assays under development.</p>
      </div>
      <ul class="kinds mt-12">
        <li>
          <h3 class="h3">Monogenic disorders</h3>
          <p>Haemoglobinopathies and musculopathies: inherited disorders of haemoglobin, and inherited conditions that weaken the muscles. The two families we have developed tests for so far.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3 class="h3">Pharmacogenetic variants</h3>
          <p>How a person's genes change their response to a medicine, for personalised therapy. In development.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3 class="h3">Rare genetic disorders</h3>
          <p>Tests for rare inherited conditions, developed when an institution needs one.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3 class="h3">Custom molecular diagnostic assays</h3>
          <p>Assays designed for a research study or a clinical service.</p>
        </li>
      </ul>

      <div class="sofar">
        <h3 class="h3">Developed so far</h3>
        <p>Each of these began with an institution that needed it. The next can begin with yours.</p>
      </div>
      {%- include "test-rows.njk" %}
    </div>
  </section>

